Description: Prefer the configured DRM render node for hardware WebRender
Forwarded: not-needed
Author: Asterinas development team

When Firefox creates the hardware WebRender EGL display, GTK may already have
an X11 display. ESR then skips the existing EGL device-enumeration path and
uses EGL_DEFAULT_DISPLAY, which the QEMU guest selects as llvmpipe. Keep the
existing fallback, but let the forceAccel WebRender request try the configured
DRM render node first. This patch is source-audited only; it requires a
provenance-tracked Firefox build before runtime use.

--- a/gfx/gl/GLLibraryEGL.cpp
+++ b/gfx/gl/GLLibraryEGL.cpp
@@ -948,7 +948,10 @@
       ret = GetAndInitSoftwareDisplay(*this, aProofOfLock);
     }
     // Initialize the display the normal way
-    if (!ret && !gdk_display_get_default() && !forceSoftware) {
+    // Hardware WebRender must prefer the configured DRM render node even
+    // when GTK has already initialized an X11 display.
+    if (!ret && (forceAccel || !gdk_display_get_default()) &&
+        !forceSoftware) {
       ret = GetAndInitDeviceDisplay(*this, aProofOfLock);
       if (!ret) {
         ret = GetAndInitSurfacelessDisplay(*this, aProofOfLock);
